// spec: LEX-025
//
// A Char is a Unicode code point: 0 .. 10FFFF, less the surrogates
// D800 .. DFFF, which encode no character.
//
// ⚠️ The range used to be 0..127, so '#233' was refused where the language
// requires 'é'.  The diagnostic has the shape every other scan error has --
// '[line N] Error: ...' -- because that is where it is detected; it used to
// arrive as a bare raise with no line and no caret, since ScanChar built the
// value by calling the Char built-in.

WriteLn (#1114112);
